pyramid as a compact image code. IEEE Trans Comm 31:532&#x02013;40; <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.citeseer.ifi.unizh.ch/burt83laplacian.html">http://www.citeseer.ifi.unizh.ch/burt83laplacian.html</ext-link>. Cited 29 March 2006</citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kunz</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Eck</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Fillbrandt</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Sonka</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Fitzpatrick</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A nonlinear multi-resolution gradient adaptive filter for medical images</article-title><source>Medical imaging, vol. 5032</source><year>2003</year><publisher-loc>San Diego, Calif</publisher-loc><publisher-name>SPIE</publisher-name><fpage>732</fpage><lpage>742</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Kunz D, Eck K, Fillbrandt H, et al (2003) A nonlinear multi-resolution gradient adaptive filter for medical images. In: Sonka M, Fitzpatrick JM (eds) Medical imaging, vol. 5032. SPIE, San Diego, pp 732&#x02013;42 </citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>